CHANGELOG
---------
# 1.2.0
* Added a thermometer showing the colors and associated temperatures
* Allowed temperature range is now -273,15 to 1.000.000 instead of -99 to 99 (all °C)

# 1.1.0 (2020-12-29)
A small, incremental update to Blackbody. Improvements:

* An error message is shown if opening a thermogram fails
* When opening fails, Blackbody doesn't unload any loaded thermograms anymore
* Added logo's heat waves as a nicer placeholder when no thermogram is opened yet
* Refined headerbar controls to only be sensitive when a thermogram is opened
* Three more known-to-be-compatible cameras (FLIR C2, FLIR E5 and FLIR P60)

# 1.0.0 (2020-12-28)
First release of Blackbody. The most important features are:

* Loading FLIR thermograms from many cameras
* Loading single-band TIFFs assumed to be in °C
* Rendering to many different colors palettes, including inferno and turbo
* Specifying the thermal range to render
* Zooming in and out
* Translated to multiple languages (English, Dutch, French, German)
* Available for Linux and Windows
